        "name": "USN-7701-3",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - Device tree and open firmware driver;   - SCSI subsystem;   - TTY drivers;   - SMB network file system;   - Bluetooth subsystem;   - Network traffic control; (CVE-2023-52975, CVE-2024-38541, CVE-2025-37797, CVE-2024-49950, CVE-2024-50073, CVE-2023-52757, CVE-2025-38083)",
